TEXT 88 -216 Left 2 ;{Vto} sets the threshold and {dir} the\n"direction"; dir=0 disables the quadratic\noperation. Despite being very fast, even\nfor kV and up, it has two elements performing\na quadratic operation, even if they are doing\nit natively.
TEXT 696 -280 Left 2 ;(a + k)^2 - 2ak - k^2 = a^2\n \nThis considers {k} as a static parameter\nrepresenting an estimation of the absolute\nmaximum value V(a) can have. Only one\nquadratic operation now, but at the cost of\nk^2 and 2*k*V(a), which might bring floating\npoint errors.
TEXT 72 368 Left 2 ;As a minor bonus, this takes advantage of\ndir=-1, which results in this being pwrs(A, 2),\nbut it's still 2xquadratic for one squaring.
TEXT 784 360 Left 2 ;The best tool for the job, even if it\nneeds {lim} as a parameter. To disable\nlim=1e308.
